## review(#238): dedupe materialise filter, reject empty objects, retarget to 0.9.4

Context: Review follow-ups on PR #238 (fix for #236 - rule triples with literal
objects dropped at materialisation). The PR was rebased onto the `0.9.4` branch
and its changelog moved from `v0.9.3` to `v0.9.4` (current pyproject version).

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py - `uri_triples`
   is now the single materialise filter: URI subject + URI predicate, literal or
   URI object, but the object must be non-empty (empty/whitespace/missing objects
   are dropped). Added a docstring explaining the rule.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py - `run_inference_task` now
   delegates to new `TwinInferredMaterialize.from_inferred` (wraps `uri_triples`) instead of re-implementing
   the same predicate (removes duplication; the two sites can no longer drift).
3. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py - parametrised test that
   empty / whitespace / missing objects, the `(batch)` placeholder subject and a
   non-URI predicate are dropped.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_background_tasks.py - test that the scheduled
   / API inference materialise path drops `(batch)` and empty-object triples while
   keeping literal ones.
5. changelogs/v0.9.4/AlexPicard10_2026-11-24.log - moved from v0.9.3 (version
   alignment).

