## review(#245): retarget to 0.9.4, Neo4j inverseOf warning, axiom-ref hardening, docs

Context: Review follow-ups on PR #245 (`owl:inverseOf` SQL inverse expansion,
#237). The PR was retargeted from `master` to `0.9.4`, rebased onto `0.9.4`
(dropping its copy of #239, already merged as 37f00273) and its changelog moved
from `v0.9.3` to `v0.9.4`.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jStore.py - the `inverse_expand` no-op now
   logs a warning (backend does not support `owl:inverseOf` expansion yet)
   instead of failing silently.
2. src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py - `_resolve_axiom_prop_uri`
   keeps only the local name of bare axiom refs containing `#` or `/`
   (`ex#p`, `a/p`), so no stray separator leaks into the predicate URI.
3. docs/architecture.md, docs/backend.md - document `inverse_expand`, the
   `graph:inverse` provenance, the `SQLGraphReasoningOps` mixin, axiom-driven
   graph reasoning and the Neo4j limitation.
4. tests - `test_neo4j_store.py` (no-op + warning, never hits the SQL default),
   `test_sql_graph_reasoning_ops.py` (GraphDBBackend inherits the mixin ops),
   `test_reasoning_service.py` (failing `inverse_expand` does not abort other
   ops, axiom ref resolution variants, mirrored/duplicate axioms deduplicated).
5. changelogs/v0.9.4/AlexPicard10_2026-11-25.log - moved from `v0.9.3`; the
   stale "tests pending" line replaced by the actual result.

